# netsurf: BBC's 24-column grids -- calc max-width, wide uniform repeats, grid item sizing (patch 347, with 347-libcss)
# Generated 2026-10-30
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser (patch stack through 346, with 347-libcss)
#
# bbc.com/news drew its lead story about 70px wide with one word per line.
# That has been so since at least r59, usually hidden under the consent
# overlay. Seven causes, each reduced against Chromium:
#
#  - layout_internal.h / layout.c: a calc-family max-width or min-width
#    went through css_unit_len2device_px(), which has no reference width,
#    so `max-width: calc(100% - 32px)` resolved to 0 (any box, not just
#    grids). The used value now resolves with css_unit_len2device_px_ref()
#    against the available width; unresolvable means no constraint. The
#    intrinsic pass skips a percentage-dependent calc as it does a plain
#    percentage, and box_has_percentage_max_width() counts calc.
#  - css_rewrite.c: the explicit track list is rewritten in place and
#    capped at 8 tracks, so `repeat(24, 1fr)` came out as 5 columns and
#    every span filled the row. A uniform flexible repeat (`repeat(N,
#    <k>fr)` or `repeat(N, minmax(0, <k>fr))`) that cannot be carried whole
#    now goes as the count form `-macsurf-grid: N`.
#  - layout_grid.c: the auto-placement occupancy map is 32 columns wide
#    (columns from 16 on read as occupied). Uniform spans and offsets use
#    the exact share instead of whole floored columns (11px short over 16
#    of 24). The justify-content rebuild is skipped for a uniform grid
#    wider than the track arrays.
#  - layout_grid.c: grid items now apply their resolved min-width and
#    max-width (both were dropped) and are offset by their own left
#    margin. `margin-inline: 16px` on BBC's page grid was lost.
#  - layout.c: a count-form grid's min-content is cols x the widest
#    single-span item's min-content plus gaps. An item spanning several
#    flexible tracks has no content-based minimum (Grid 6.6). Taking the
#    widest item made `min-width: fit-content` card grids as wide as one
#    nowrap headline.
#  - layout.c: in the intrinsic pass `min-width: fit-content` floors the
#    min-content contribution at min-content, not max-content (CSS Sizing
#    3).
#  - css_rewrite.c: `grid-column-end` / `grid-row-end: span N` longhands.
#  - css_rewrite.c: the placement declaration carries its axes mask for
#    347-libcss.
#
# Gate: CSS-grid-uniform-placement (GRIDUNI347 9/9, Chromium 9/9, 1px
# tolerance). Before the patch, legs 1-4 and 6-9 failed. Inline-style grid
# placement (style="grid-column: ...") is still not rewritten; that is a
# known separate gap (fixes817e).
